## SOLID

- **SRP:** one struct, one job
- **OCP:** extend via new port implementations, don't touch orchestration core
- **LSP:** implementations honor full port contract
- **ISP:** narrow ports — no god-objects
- **DIP:** domain depends on `ports.*` abstractions only

## Clean Code

- Names reveal intent. Booleans: `is`/`has`/`can` prefix.
- Functions do ONE thing. Early return over nesting.
- No hidden side effects. No speculative abstractions (YAGNI).
- Comments: WHY only, never WHAT. No godoc on self-explanatory functions.
- Errors: return always, wrap with `%w`. Never `log.Fatal` in library code.

## Testing

- TDD: failing test first, minimal implementation second.
- Table-driven tests. Always `-race`.
- No real network — `httptest.NewServer` or injected stubs.
- `t.Skip` for integration tests needing external credentials.
- Run inside sub-module: `cd redis && go test ./... -race`

## Security Invariants

- SSRF: `netutil.ValidateURL` before any outbound HTTP
- Body limits: `io.LimitReader` — no bare `io.ReadAll`
- API keys: SHA-256 + `crypto/subtle.ConstantTimeCompare`
- Rate limit all unauthenticated endpoints
- Hard cap on in-memory maps growing from external input

## Go Rules

- Propagate caller `ctx` — no mid-chain `context.Background()`
- Cleanup goroutines: `context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)`
- Sentinel errors exported; error factories unexported
- `sync.RWMutex` for read-heavy state

## Commits

```
feat(fiber): description
fix(redis): description
test(gemini): description
```

No AI attribution. No co-author trailers.

## Absolute Don'ts

- `log.Fatal` in library code
- `io.ReadAll(resp.Body)` without LimitReader
- Outbound HTTP without SSRF validation
- Importing infrastructure from domain
- Sub-modules importing each other
- `context.Background()` replacing caller context
- Skipping `-race` in tests
